From 1a59905e6dd9dd0583bbbbac86e9f23ce655d85e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:29:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: port the calibrated MSM8926 CPU domain

Join calibration, canonical OPP filtering, retry-safe attachment,
reference-clock selection and verified startup normalization. Refresh
both PLL parents before guarding every APC request with the actual
reported CPU rate. Retain rail ownership and feedback state across
recoverable failures; resume waits for a fresh nominal request.

The incoming domain retains the older fork rails wrapper. Reconcile its
separate fuse allocation into the incoming flexible array sized with
struct_size. Preserve those responsibilities, with calibrated
eligibility, ownership, failure rollback and publication. Keep the LTS
allocation spelling and correct indentation without changing tokens.
Host models do not prove actual collapse, wake voltage or secure firmware.

Backport as part of the initial maintained-6.18.63 CPU stack. The complete
series passes 45 selected host test methods. Standalone executables use
ASan, UBSan and normal LeakSanitizer; ctypes numerical oracles are
explicitly unsanitized. Twenty selected objects compile with the feature
enabled and disabled on ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT (120 objects), W=1 and
nonpermissive CFI, with no diagnostics. ARM32 RT is unsupported.

Original author/date and source notices are preserved. Codex prepared
this local backport and verification. Original scoped source provenance
remains recorded in the review evidence. Human review and DCO remain
pending; no phone, publication or maintainer action has occurred.

Backported from commit 4569dae3b15824cb1d1fa0e388ba727bd52d6102 ("pmdomain:
qcom: port the calibrated MSM8926 CPU domain")
